Relevant columns and their potential use  
• GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.YEAR._2023  
  – "type": event category; filter for 'PullRequestEvent'.  
  – "payload": JSON text that holds the "action" field; filter for `"action":"opened"` (i.e., creation of a pull request).  
  – "created_at": Unix‑epoch time (µs); restrict to 18‑Jan‑2023 (00:00–23:59 UTC).  
  – "repo": VARIANT object; field "name" gives repository‑name for joining.  

• GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.GITHUB_REPOS.LANGUAGES  
  – "repo_name": repository name; join key to YEAR._2023."repo":"name".  
  – "language": VARIANT array with all languages of the repo; test whether one of the array elements equals 'JavaScript'.  

Typical conditions that will be used  
```
y."type" = 'PullRequestEvent'
AND y."created_at" BETWEEN 1674000000000000 AND 1674086399000000   -- 18‑Jan‑2023 UTC (µs)
AND y."payload":"action"::STRING = 'opened'
AND l_lang.value::STRING = 'JavaScript'
AND l."repo_name" = y."repo":"name"::STRING
```


Ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each returns ≤20 rows)

```sql
--1. Description: Show 20 repos whose language list (as a string) contains the substring 'JavaScript'.
SELECT "repo_name", "language"::STRING
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"
WHERE "language"::STRING ILIKE '%JavaScript%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--2. Description: Flatten the language array and list one row per language element (proof that 'JavaScript' exists).
SELECT "repo_name",
       lang.value::STRING AS "one_language"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES" l,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => l."language") lang
WHERE lang.index < 3          -- show first few elements only
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--3. Description: Look at distinct event types that happened on 18‑Jan‑2023.
SELECT DISTINCT y."type"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."YEAR"."_2023" y
WHERE y."created_at" BETWEEN 1674000000000000 AND 1674086399000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--4. Description: Pull out some raw "payload" values for PullRequestEvent records on the target day.
SELECT y."payload"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."YEAR"."_2023" y
WHERE y."type" = 'PullRequestEvent'
  AND y."created_at" BETWEEN 1674000000000000 AND 1674086399000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--5. Description: Inspect action values inside the payload JSON for PullRequestEvent rows.
SELECT y."payload":"action"::STRING AS "action",
       y."payload":"pull_request":"merged"::BOOLEAN AS "merged?"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."YEAR"."_2023" y
WHERE y."type" = 'PullRequestEvent'
  AND y."created_at" BETWEEN 1674000000000000 AND 1674086399000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--6. Description: Grab repositories involved in pull‑request *creation* events (action='opened') on 18‑Jan‑2023.
SELECT y."repo":"name"::STRING AS "repo_name",
       y."created_at"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."YEAR"."_2023" y
WHERE y."type" = 'PullRequestEvent'
  AND y."payload":"action"::STRING = 'opened'
  AND y."created_at" BETWEEN 1674000000000000 AND 1674086399000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--7. Description: Join those events with the LANGUAGES table to see which of them have JavaScript among their languages.
SELECT y."repo":"name"::STRING           AS "repo_name",
       y."created_at"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."YEAR"."_2023"            y
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES" l
     ON l."repo_name" = y."repo":"name"::STRING
     , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => l."language")       l_lang
WHERE y."type"   = 'PullRequestEvent'
  AND y."payload":"action"::STRING = 'opened'
  AND y."created_at" BETWEEN 1674000000000000 AND 1674086399000000
  AND l_lang.value::STRING = 'JavaScript'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--8. Description: Count pull‑request creation events per repo (JavaScript repos only) for 18‑Jan‑2023.
SELECT y."repo":"name"::STRING                         AS "repo_name",
       COUNT(*)                                        AS "pr_open_events"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."YEAR"."_2023"            y
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES" l
     ON l."repo_name" = y."repo":"name"::STRING
     , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => l."language")       l_lang
WHERE y."type"   = 'PullRequestEvent'
  AND y."payload":"action"::STRING = 'opened'
  AND y."created_at" BETWEEN 1674000000000000 AND 1674086399000000
  AND l_lang.value::STRING = 'JavaScript'
GROUP BY "repo_name"
ORDER BY "pr_open_events" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--9. Description: Show distinct repositories that meet all criteria (proof of join cardinality).
SELECT DISTINCT y."repo":"name"::STRING AS "repo_name"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."YEAR"."_2023"            y
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES" l
     ON l."repo_name" = y."repo":"name"::STRING
     , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => l."language")       l_lang
WHERE y."type"   = 'PullRequestEvent'
  AND y."payload":"action"::STRING = 'opened'
  AND y."created_at" BETWEEN 1674000000000000 AND 1674086399000000
  AND l_lang.value::STRING = 'JavaScript'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--10. Description: Obtain the grand total number of pull‑request creation events on 18‑Jan‑2023 for JavaScript repos.
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "total_pr_creation_events"
FROM (
      SELECT y.*
      FROM "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."YEAR"."_2023"            y
      JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES" l
           ON l."repo_name" = y."repo":"name"::STRING
           , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => l."language")       l_lang
      WHERE y."type"   = 'PullRequestEvent'
        AND y."payload":"action"::STRING = 'opened'
        AND y."created_at" BETWEEN 1674000000000000 AND 1674086399000000
        AND l_lang.value::STRING = 'JavaScript'
     ) AS sub;
```

